      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Possession (1981) stands as one of cinema's most visceral explorations of divorce and psychological breakdown. Director Andrzej Żuławski created this fever dream during his own divorce, channeling raw emotional trauma into a genre-defying horror-drama. The film's infamous subway scene, where Isabelle Adjani convulses in an underground tunnel, rewrites the rules of physical performance in horror. It shares DNA with other boundary-pushing films of its era like <a href=\"/movie/28942\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"28942\">The Brood</a> (1979) and <a href=\"/movie/11542\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"11542\">Altered States</a> (1980), where personal crisis manifests as body horror."
      },
