      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Possession's influence looms large over the New French Extremity movement of the 2000s. Films like <a href=\"/movie/40723\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"40723\">Trouble Every Day</a> (2001) and <a href=\"/movie/1836\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1836\">In My Skin</a> (2002) echo its combination of body horror and psychological exploration. The movement's emphasis on transgressive sexuality and violent transformation owes a clear debt to Żuławski's masterpiece. The film's DNA can be seen in contemporary works like <a href=\"/movie/530385\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"530385\">Midsommar</a> (2019) and <a href=\"/movie/503919\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"503919\">The Lighthouse</a> (2019), where relationship breakdown intersects with cosmic horror."
      }
